sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Farhadifar et al. (2007) Drosophila wing disc apical vertex model, Lewis's law packing & PCP (Fz/Stbm) hinge-contraction vertex dynamics — MorphoEval overall 84.8/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py` (84.8/100, down from 90.9 in Pass 2). The single v2 remediation item is closed: Section 2b adds a genuine vertex model (tri-cellular vertices, analytic forces of Farhadifar Eq. 1 verified by finite differences, T1 exchanges) coupled to an explicit per-bond Frizzled/Strabismus asymmetry tensor with zero trace and perpendicular cancellation (Lean theorem 5), driven by a pupal hinge-contraction pure-shear strain with an Etournay-style shear decomposition (Lean theorem 6). At eps_pcp = 0.5 the model gives a cell-elongation peak <|Q|> = 0.253 (Etournay 2015 ~0.25, approx.), 20 T1s all on AP-oriented junctions versus 11 in the eps_pcp = 0 control, a rearrangement share of tissue shear of 0.307 (vs 0.165 control), bond-tension anisotropy Lambda_AP/Lambda_PD = 2.39 and a monotonic eps_pcp sweep. The re-score is lower because the audit now records what the v2 scores overlooked: the Section 2 regimes are Lloyd relaxations whose Lewis's-law fit is imposed by a post-hoc area reweighting, the only vendored specimen is a mouse epithelium, three new DOIs and all new reference values are unverified offline, and the PCP effect on hexagon fraction has the opposite sign to Classen et al. (2005). Overall 84.8/100 (faithfulness 83.1, reproducibility 88.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 7e4f207; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 85, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 91, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 86, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 91. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_wing_vertex_model_comparison.png: rendered output of 2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py at 7e4f207, image/png, 1297705 B, 3075×1935 px, artifact_sha256 2cb99062ead6793102bd757b45c1c91c5b484d3f97e6a67b428f78f2fbb36aa7 (sha256 2cb99062ead6793102bd757b45c1c91c5b484d3f97e6a67b428f78f2fbb36aa7), spec_fingerprint 00f70e92aaa338b22956554153bb93fbccd372cdaae2e3f47f4744bcadfffe52. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 00f70e92aaa338b22956554153bb93fbccd372cdaae2e3f47f4744bcadfffe52; artifact_sha256: 2cb99062ead6793102bd757b45c1c91c5b484d3f97e6a67b428f78f2fbb36aa7. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Farhadifar, Röper, Aigouy, Eaton & Jülicher (2007) Current Biology Eqs. 1-2 & Fig. 2A: apical epithelial vertex energy functional E({r_i}) = sum (K/2)(A_alpha - A^(0))^2 + sum Lambda_{ij} l_{ij} + sum (Gamma/2) L_alpha^2 parameterized by (Lambda_bar, Gamma_bar), partitioning ground states into Case I (rigid hexagonal, canonical wing disc Lambda_bar=0.12, Gamma_bar=0.04), Case II (soft network), and Case III (cell collapse). | Farhadifar et al. (2007) Fig. 3-4, Gibson et al. (2006) Nature & Classen et al. (2005) Dev. Cell: proliferating 3rd-instar Drosophila wing disc exhibits P(6) approx 0.455 and obeys Lewis's Law <A_n>/<A> = (n-2)/4, whereas post-mitotic pupal wing annealing increases P(6) to ~0.78, and PCP (fz, stbm) mutants fail to reach wild-type hexagonal order. | Aigouy et al. (2010) Cell & Etournay et al. (2015) eLife: hinge contraction from ~15 hAPF stretches the blade along the proximal-distal axis, cells elongate along PD and then relax through oriented cell rearrangements while the Fz/Stbm PCP axis reorients to PD; tissue shear decomposes into cell-elongation change plus rearrangement, division and correlation contributions.; reconstructed_in_script: 2D periodic Voronoi-seed (Lloyd-type) packing and mitotic cleavage simulation across 4 regimes (Proliferating Wing Disc, Post-Mitotic Pupal Wing, High-Contractility Case I, Soft Case II), 2D (Lambda_bar, Gamma_bar) phase diagram, UV laser junction ablation recoil curves, and 7-point continuous Lambda_bar sweep (Section 2, panels A1-A4, B1-B5). | Pass 3: explicit tri-cellular vertex model (analytic forces of Eq. 1, T1 exchanges) on a 100-cell patch with a per-bond Frizzled/Strabismus asymmetry tensor Q_ab modulating line tension Lambda_ab = Lambda_bar (1 + eps_pcp n.Q_ab.n), Fz-Stbm feedback + flow-alignment polarity dynamics, an area-preserving hinge-contraction boundary strain diag(lambda, 1/lambda) with ln lambda = 0.35, shear decomposition into cell-elongation and rearrangement parts, a PCP loss-of-function (eps_pcp = 0) control and a 6-point eps_pcp sweep (Section 2b, panels C1-C5, GIF panel 4). | Junction-guided Voronoi-watershed segmentation of the vendored apical junction-stained polygonal epithelial micrograph (N=37 interior cells, P(6)=0.4865, P(n) correlation r = 0.9913 against the Farhadifar wing-disc distribution).; transfer_boundary: 2D apical junctional projection of 3D pseudostratified/columnar wing imaginal disc epithelial cells. | The vendored specimen `drosophila_wing_epithelium_specimen.jpg` is a Wikimedia Commons epithelial monolayer whose scout manifest records organism Mus musculus; its polygon statistics are compared with Drosophila literature values as a cross-species epithelial-packing transfer, not as a Drosophila specimen. | The Section 2 regimes are Voronoi-seed relaxations with a post-hoc Lewis's-law area reweighting and a hexagonal-lattice pull in the pupal regime; only Section 2b integrates the Farhadifar energy on vertex degrees of freedom. | The PCP coupling sign (PCP-complex-bearing AP junctions stiffened for eps_pcp > 0), the polarity-dynamics gains (k_fb = 0.6, k_flow = 0.4), the initial polarity spread (0.6 rad) and the hinge log-strain (0.35) are modelling choices, not fitted to data; Pass 3 reference values from Etournay (2015) and Classen (2005) are approximate figure reads recorded offline.; does_not_claim: Does not model basal extracellular matrix curvature, 3D apico-basal scutoid transitions, Fat/Dachsous polarity, the pre-15 hAPF margin-directed PCP pattern, cell divisions or extrusions during pupal morphogenesis, the hinge as a separate mechanical compartment, or periodic boundary conditions for the explicit vertex model (the patch is clamped at its margin). | Does not claim to reproduce the Classen et al. (2005) PCP-mutant loss of hexagonal order: in this model the PCP coupling lowers the final hexagon fraction (sign mismatch disclosed in measurement `pcp_wt_minus_mutant_hexagonal_fraction_delta`).." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py:1765-1771 and 774-1023 — the PCP coupling lowers the final hexagon fraction (P(6) 0.867 -> 0.733 for eps_pcp 0 -> 0.5) whereas Classen et al. (2005) report the opposite; add the PCP-dependent junction remodeling/annealing step (post-T1 junction regrowth and polarity-dependent tension relaxation) and a longer post-contraction relaxation window, then re-test the sign of `pcp_wt_minus_mutant_hexagonal_fraction_delta`.",
            "remediation needed: 2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py:401-405 and 378-379 — remove the post-hoc Lewis's-law area reweighting (`adjusted_areas = areas * (1 + 0.14 * gamma_slope_boost * (n - 6))`) and the hexagonal-lattice pull (`0.042 * hex_disp`) from `simulate_vertex_regime`, and re-derive panels A1-A4 / measurements 1-7 from the Section 2b explicit vertex model (periodic version with division) so Lewis's law and pupal hexagonal order are emergent rather than imposed.",
            "remediation needed: 2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py:533-567 and 846-848 — replace the clamped non-periodic patch by a periodic explicit vertex model with an affine box deformation so boundary cells participate in the mechanics, and add the Sugimura & Ishihara (2013) force-inference tension anisotropy as a quantitative comparison for `tension_anisotropy_ratio`.",
            "remediation needed: 2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py:782-785, 931 and 523-524 — expose k_feedback, k_flow, init_polarity_sigma and the T1 thresholds on the CLI, cite or fit them (Aigouy 2010 polarity-alignment time scale; Farhadifar 2007 l_T1), and render the hinge-strain sweep (gamma_PD in [0, 0.5]) as a panel rather than leaving it in development notes.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/drosophila_wing_vertex_model/drosophila_wing_vertex_model_reference.json:192-252 — the Etournay (2015) |Q| peak 0.25 and ~0.5 rearrangement share, the Classen (2005) 0.78 / 0.60 hexagon fractions and the three new DOIs are offline figure reads; digitise the Etournay Fig. 3 shear curves and the Classen polygon histograms into a pinned table, resolve the DOIs, and replace the `provenance: approximate` flags.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/drosophila_wing_vertex_model/scout_manifest.json:8 and drosophila_wing_vertex_model_reference.json:54-62 — the vendored specimen is a Mus musculus epithelium; vendor a genuine Drosophila pupal-wing or wing-disc micrograph (e.g. a CC-BY panel from Etournay et al. 2015 eLife or Aigouy et al. 2010 if licence permits), pin its SHA-256, segment it, and record the species consistently in JSON, README and file name." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.848"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (Pass 3 builder + primary re-assessor, autonomous loop slot-043)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

